  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Big coast to coast – counter-attack via jokers",
  "description": "Split the players into four teams. Two teams play 3-on-3 with goalies over the full rink, and the other two teams are jokers in passing zones along the boards – one joker team in each half of the rink (marked J). Each team's jokers stand in the half that team defends.\n\nOne team attacks. When the defending team wins the puck, it must first pass to one of its jokers, and from there it launches a fast counter-attack towards the other net. The puck stays in play until the defenders have found a joker. Each team plays one attack and one defence, then the teams switch – after a goal or when the puck leaves play. Rotate the playing teams and the joker teams too. Goalies are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "As soon as you win the puck: look up and find the nearest joker."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Players without the puck skate straight up ice towards the far net – not sideways."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass in front of the skater so they can take the puck at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish quickly, before the opponents are back in defence."
    }
  ],
